WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.570
Jamitov Hymem.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.880
This man is the founder of the Titans.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.520
Learning of the A.E.U.G.'s invasion
of Jaburo...

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:51.820
...he journeyed to space
for the observation of Gryps.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.990
Gryps is divided into two colonies...

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.600
...and is about to be situated
close to Luna II.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:10.700
Plans to fortify the Titans are underway.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.860
Shuttle Launch

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.340
I'm amazed they made it here.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.380
Hello, Amuro!

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.650
Fraw Kobayashi, Katz, Letz!

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.580
And Kikka, too!

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.120
- You all look well.
- You haven't changed one bit, Amuro.

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:04.560
Thank you.

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:06.620
You're just as I remember you.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.960
You've really grown, Katz!

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.070
What's up?

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:13.300
I've got so many things to tell you.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.360
Do you mind if we stay over?

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.870
It would be my pleasure, Fraw.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.080
Miss, we have some very fresh beef,
unless you'd rather have something else.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.320
Thank you, that sounds great!

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.820
- Master Letz?
- Not for me.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.960
At six months, you need to be
extra careful, don't you?

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.130
I'm well past the insecure stages.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.260
You really know very little
about these things.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.540
Get married. Then you'll...!

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.040
Do you think the Forces would allow me?

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.770
You still have the hots for Sayla, right?

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:57.840
Stop hiding within your shell.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.750
Many youngsters have arrived
in Cheyenne.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.150
I barely have enough time
to look them over.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:04.690
Why aren't you going to Jaburo, Mr. Amuro?

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:05.890
Huh?

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.570
Then does your servant couple
also belong to the Forces?

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.430
They say they applied
after seeing an ad for the position...

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.700
...but they're no doubt soldiers
here to keep an eye on me.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.240
You seem relieved, Mother.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:29.800
Of course.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.470
He hasn't changed, after all.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:32.850
Are you saying that you have changed,
Mother?

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:34.150
Perhaps.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:38.150
For one, I can eat at will in public
without wondering what others might think.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.190
But it's important that you eat,
now more than ever, right?

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:41.850
You're right.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.590
My father realized what was happening
at Jaburo...

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.930
...and went to assist
as a member of Karaba.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.370
So, what are you doing here?

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:53.860
I'm unaware of any organization
by the name of Karaba.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.340
How about the A.E.U.G.?

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.740
Nothing more than what's been covered
on the news.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.800
Then how about joining Karaba?!

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:00.840
Mr. Amuro?!

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:05.110
If you didn't have anybody
in the shadows like me...

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.150
...you guys wouldn't have had
a place to run to.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.350
We didn't run away to you!

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:13.480
We did as we were told
only to protect Mother!

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:14.530
Katz!

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.690
You're going along
with the Forces' demands...

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.200
...because you're afraid to lose
this life of yours!

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.530
Katz! That will be enough!

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.570
Stay out of this, Mother!

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.100
Life here is hell.

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:27.140
Mr. Amuro!

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.170
Doesn't it bother you that
you're being told off by a child like me?!

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.310
The supervision of the Earth Federation
Government is presently quite loose!

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.110
Please tell me the truth!

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.700
There's no way he can speak his mind!

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.220
You don't realize the capabilities
of the military!

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.550
It's because the Earth Federation Forces
are wavering...

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.680
...that the Titans can have their way!

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.220
I fought more than my share
during the One Year War, Katz!

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:50.890
But you are still young!

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:53.390
As a Newtype, I'm looked upon
as a dangerous element...

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.400
...and therefore confined to these premises.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.060
I know that!

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:59.400
Then can't you understand the tendency
for a person to become a little lazy...

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.560
...with these living conditions
forced upon him?!

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:07.010
To us... or more so to Mother,
you were a hero, Mr. Amuro.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:12.440
Please stop telling me this nonsense...

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.040
...and at least say there's a mobile suit
hidden underground, or something!

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.140
Katz! Stop it!

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.520
All right!

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.450
We'll leave tomorrow.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.160
To where?

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.390
We plan to go to Japan.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.930
Are you able to leave the country,
in your position?

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.960
For some reason,
I was able to get a visa.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:35.600
As Katz says, I guess that's a proof
that the government's been slacking off.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:38.740
- How about tickets?
- Sorry.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:42.270
We were initially planning to stay here
for four or five days, so not yet.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.650
Okay, I'll make arrangements
for you tomorrow.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:46.980
Thank you.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:55.720
I'm sorry for the child's impertinence.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:07.870
<i>Is Kennedy Airport safe,</i>
<i>Hayato Kobayashi?</i>

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:10.030
<i>It's presently under Karaba's control.</i>

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:12.130
Karaba... I don't like it.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:12.970
Why not?

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:15.010
Sounds like a name for some secret society!

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:39.430
Director Hayato. Welcome, sir!

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.990
There are about forty pilots
who we need to get back to space!

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.700
We have two shuttles,
so we should be fine, but...!

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:45.740
What is it?

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.900
We only have one shuttle pilot.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.310
Understood.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.080
Hey! Gundam Mk. II pilot!

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:55.120
Do you have any idea
where Kai Shiden might be?

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:59.020
Mr. Kai went over to Customs
with Miss Reccoa!

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:00.390
Thank you!

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:02.350
Take me there.

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:05.730
I welcome you,
as a member of the A.E.U.G.!

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:07.350
Thank you.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:08.400
Mr. Kai!

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.330
How are things coming along
with the Lieutenant?

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:18.040
I didn't realize that
the Karaba organization was this big.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:20.770
I'd like to say "naturally", however,
we can no longer use this place.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.380
Because we allowed
the two Garudas to land.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:26.120
- What'll you do?
- We'll move to Northern Europe maybe.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.890
Could you possibly arrange a shuttle pilot?

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:32.920
Roger!

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:53.940
Where could Kai have gone
without even dropping by to say "hi"?

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.340
Make sure fuel shipment
is completed in thirty minutes!

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:01.750
We're certain the enemy will be here!

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:03.250
The Argama will come for it, right?

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.220
This is a swell time to be telling me that!

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:06.810
What's wrong?

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:09.160
They say Oakland's Newtype Lab
is now controlled by the Titans.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.180
The Newtype Lab?

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.350
That's not good.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:13.590
Oh, Director Hayato!

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:17.100
Just now, a tall person
asked me to give this to you.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:18.500
Thank you.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:20.400
It's from Kai.

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:29.610
So Kai's planning to collect information
on his own.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:33.510
"Lieutenant Quattro is likely
Char Aznable."

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:37.610
"It is a cowardly action on Char's part
to use a false name...

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:40.320
...to fight against
the Earth Federation Government."

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.190
So you won't work with him.

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:50.360
Not yet?

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.270
No! It's come in!

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:53.670
A telegram from the Argama!

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.470
Decryption code 33.

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:56.970
That's correct, it's them.

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:02.370
"Although orbit change is possible,
we're in a battle with an enemy ship."

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.810
But it says they'll make it
to the rendezvous point.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.780
Meaning the enemy's attacks are scattered.

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:10.950
Are you aware that the Argama's
present captain is Bright Noa?

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:12.390
Formerly of the White Base?

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.050
That's right.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:16.390
In that case they'll be able
to make the rendezvous while battling!

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:17.950
Exactly.

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:20.500
Calculate the rendezvous point
and time for launch!

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:21.860
Yes, sir!

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:24.030
We have it!

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:26.400
The best time for take-off
is forty minutes from now!

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.130
I can't imagine they're joking.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:30.370
- Are the shuttles ready for take-off?
- Just a moment.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.670
Shuttle launch is in thirty-nine minutes!
You can do it, right?!

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.710
These lift off shuttles are items
for the museum! That's impossible!

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.610
- We can fuel it in time!
- Shut up.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:43.680
We're also launching the mobile suit shuttle
at the same time. You can do it, I presume.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.810
Who's that fool talking?!
Two launches at once? It can't be done!

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:50.220
We don't want our new model mobile suits
to fall into the Titans' hands.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.960
- <i>Don't blame me if they collide!</i>
- We'll control that.

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:55.020
- <i>Then let's see you do it.</i>
- Roger!

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.730
- I'm glad we can do it.
- Sure.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:01.840
Apolly, where are you?!

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:05.140
Lieutenant Roberto, forget about
erasing the combat memory panel!

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:07.670
What?! But we need to change it
for Earth battle...

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.710
...for it to be any use to Karaba!

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.240
It's more important that you guys
make it back to space.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:13.040
What is it?!

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:15.020
We're short of pilots!
Take a seat in the shuttle!

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:15.880
Huh?

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:17.580
Rely on your experience
as a veteran in that line!

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:18.920
I've never experienced anything <i>that</i> old!

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.520
- We have no time! Hurry!
- R-Right!

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:23.390
When are we boarding the shuttle?!

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.450
Start loading the mobile suits right now!

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.260
We're taking the Gundam Mk. II,
Hyaku Shiki...

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:29.300
...and Roberto's Rick Dias back with us!

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:30.460
Yes!

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:32.090
What about <i>my</i> Rick Dias?

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:34.430
Sorry, but we'll leave it with Karaba!
Go on!

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:35.730
You're kidding!

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:37.740
- Who's piloting the shuttle?!
- I am!

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:39.440
- Hurry over to the jeep!
- Yes, sir!

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.570
Director Hayato, is something the matter?

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:43.480
I'm done with what I needed to do.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:46.020
Please let me hear your opinion
about this later.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.680
- Is this it?!
- Yes, sir!

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:52.850
No guarantees!

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:59.950
Oh, boy. Does this thing really fly?

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:32.990
In accordance with our information...

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.530
...over there, the A.E.U.G. are acting
like they're something special, huh?

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:44.240
- See you later, Lieutenant!
- Later!

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:46.210
Make sure the mobile suits get loaded!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.170
- See you later, Kamille.
- See you!

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:56.050
We'll start loading the mobile suits
onto the freighter now!

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.150
- Got that?!
- <i>We're ready!</i>

00:12:58.220 --> 00:12:59.950
<i>I think we should get a move on!</i>

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:01.120
<i>Roger!</i>

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:05.760
Roberto, that's enough!

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:07.490
Hurry with the Rick Dias transfer!

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.970
Yes! I'm almost done.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:13.530
- Kamille, your Gundam as well!
- Yes, sir!

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:16.040
This letter has nothing to do with me.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:19.570
Kai says you are Char Aznable.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.410
Is that the truth?

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.670
You're overrating my abilities.

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:26.480
Besides, why would Zeon's Char
bother to help the A.E.U.G.?

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.680
The Zabi family perished seven years ago.

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:34.380
In which case I can see Char shifting
his attention to rebuilding Earth.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:38.890
It wouldn't surprise me to find him returning
to Earth and helping the A.E.U.G..

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.260
Let's say for a moment that I am Char.

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:43.320
What's your point?

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.690
Please hurry!

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:48.240
If you recall from Kai's letter, he says...

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:52.000
..."Char has the caliber to be a leader,
yet will not. That makes him a coward."

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:55.610
By taking the easy way out, and
participating only as a mobile suit pilot...

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.480
...Char's only dishonoring himself.

00:13:57.550 --> 00:14:00.180
If Char is that type of person,
then perhaps what Kai says is true.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.690
Whether it takes ten, twenty years...

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:05.120
...you should try to become leader
of the Earth Federation Government.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:08.450
However, I am Lieutenant Quattro Bajeena.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:09.580
If that's true...!

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:11.690
Then you're a coward!

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:14.490
Char Aznable, you'd feel much better
if you let out the truth!

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:16.890
Move the Gundam over to the shuttle!

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:18.400
I will!

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:20.330
So which is it?! Please tell me!

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:26.870
I don't see any harm in acknowledging it.

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:30.980
Right now... I am
Lieutenant Quattro Bajeena.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:32.780
No more, and no less.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:36.140
Clench your teeth!

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.950
I'll "correct" adults like you!

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:45.480
<i>That's what it is to be young.</i>

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:51.960
I don't know what reasons you may have...!

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:55.670
Understand that humans
have the heart to feel shame...!

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.090
We'll attack at once.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:14.180
They're trying to escape with shuttles!

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.730
We'll prevent their launch,
and capture the A.E.U.G. mobile suits!

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.670
All units! Start up the Audhumla!

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.320
Continue the countdown!

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:47.380
<i>We intend to, don't worry!</i>

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:53.290
<i>We'll take off as planned! All of you</i>
<i>on board are to abide by my orders!</i>

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:54.490
Don't move!

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.430
What a big shot.

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:57.230
That's right.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:59.570
For the time being, I am your captain!

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.670
Countdown is continuing, is it?!

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:03.300
There's no need to wait for us!

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:04.640
- <i>It's continuing!</i>
- Good!

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.060
They're responding very quickly!

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.830
I take it that A.E.U.G. pilots
are on board that shuttle!

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:40.740
Because you get in the way!

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.210
Why'd they choose to come now?!

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:55.020
<i>One minute to lift off!</i>

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:58.090
You're not getting any closer!

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:08.730
Take this!

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:20.750
A shame we're not in space!

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:50.780
It transforms into a mobile suit!

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:59.050
That was ugly!

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:00.020
Don't take me lightly!

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.160
<i>Thirty seconds to take-off!</i>

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:14.800
What the...!

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:24.450
What?! Don't think you can win
on body size alone!

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:27.780
This isn't just for appearance!

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:34.390
What?!

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:39.290
Mr. Roberto!

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:53.840
<i>Lift off in...</i>
<i>Seven! Six!</i>

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:54.640
Five seconds!

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.580
<i>Four... three...</i>

00:18:57.050 --> 00:18:57.980
<i>Two!</i>

00:18:58.050 --> 00:18:59.850
Ready... go!

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.550
You're not going anywhere!

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:21.430
- <i>Kamille!</i>
- Yes!

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.440
- <i>Get on the Hyaku Shiki's shoulders!</i>
- Huh?

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:25.770
- <i>Get on the Hyaku Shiki's shoulders!</i>
- Yes!

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:30.600
- Release full power!
- <i>Yes!</i>

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:41.720
Say your prayers!

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:50.900
The Gundam?

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:52.460
A new model?!

00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:57.040
Damn.

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:08.020
Right there!

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:22.760
Get in here, Lieutenant Quattro!

00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:29.570
Can Kamille make it here?!

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:32.240
Come on, Mk. II!

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:40.680
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:58.330
<i>Regroup the survivors</i>
<i>and get Kennedy Port under control!</i>

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:01.260
<i>Force out the A.E.U.G. mobile suits</i>
<i>remaining on the Sudori!</i>

00:21:01.910 --> 00:21:04.500
<i>The Sudori is now under the control</i>
<i>of the Buran platoon!</i>

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:07.170
Don't think you guys can escape
the American Continent.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.480
Thank you very much, Lieutenant!

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:17.780
You did a good job yourself.

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:20.350
But Lieutenant Roberto...!

00:21:20.890 --> 00:21:22.450
He was a great pilot.

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:24.590
But this is a war.

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:25.790
This is unbearable.

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:29.030
Exactly. However, there's no time
to indulge in sentiment.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:32.090
With this many comrades,
we can still fight sufficiently.

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:34.000
We should hurry with the checkup
and repair of our equipment.

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:34.870
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.130
And where is the Audhumla headed?

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:38.870
We're headed for Hickory.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:39.810
Hickory?

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:42.600
If that doesn't work out,
we'll go to our next plan.

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:45.410
We have Karaba comrades
close to Vandenberg.

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:46.620
That's amazing to hear.

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:48.780
We'll need to replenish as well.

00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:50.440
That explains it.

00:21:50.520 --> 00:21:54.220
The Earth Federation Government
has enemies even here on Earth.

00:21:56.890 --> 00:22:00.830
<i>Why is it that people don't realize how</i>
<i>rebuilding a civilization on Earth...</i>

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:03.060
<i>...will end up polluting it again?</i>

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:07.560
<i>And it is senseless to harm each other</i>
<i>over something like this.</i>

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:16.870
- We're here! We're here!
- Congratulations, Apolly!

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:22.110
With this, their invasion operation
on Jaburo was concluded.

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:29.080
With this operation, the world learned that
unlike the main Forces up until that point...

00:22:29.560 --> 00:22:34.160
...two factions of the Earth Federation
Forces had begun fighting each other.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.330 --> 00:23:49.230
Amuro's soul, which had been
in a deep sleep, is awakened...

00:23:49.300 --> 00:23:51.270
...and he heads to the Audhumla with Katz.

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:56.400
The Gundam Mk. II struggles against
the transformable mobile suit, Asshimar.

00:23:56.470 --> 00:23:59.000
Then, Amuro suddenly appears
before Asshimar...

00:23:59.340 --> 00:24:03.010
...and old adversaries from
the past meet again here on Earth.

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:07.550
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Amuro Flies Again".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Amuro Flies Again

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:11.390
You will see the tears of time.
